==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:Guitar picks DSC06879.jpg|thumb|Plectra alias picks]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|plectron}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|plēctrum|notext=1}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|πλῆκτρον||anything to strike with, an instrument for striking the lyre, a spear point}}, from {{m|grc|πλήσσειν||to strike, to smite, to sting}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈplɛk.tɹəm/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-plectrum.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|plectra}}

# {{lb|en|music}} A small piece of plastic, metal, ivory, etc., for [[pluck]]ing the [[string]]s of a [[guitar]], [[lyre]], [[mandolin]], etc.
# {{lb|en|anatomy|zoology}} An [[anatomical]] part resembling a plectrum in shape.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|guitar pick}}
* {{l|en|pick}} (US)

